acceptance_criteria: Seven CLI and SDK operations; complete exact feasible coverage witnesses; native guarded storage; public proof; all release gates.
comments[26]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T18:17:25.406Z",codex-agent,"Companion reference: pm-cli-website-c98t. Source specification and comments read only. Implement the complete production v1 slice; strength above two and autonomous execution remain follow-ups."
  "2026-11-06T19:11:25.139Z",codex-agent,"Implementation and evidence are complete for local first-release review. Companion pm-cli-website-c98t remains read-only. Package-owned links identify source, docs and tests; public harness receipt proves three selected upstream tests and one reproduced historical regression. Required final validation commands are npm run release:check and bun run release:check with isolated Git identity configuration. No repository creation, pushing, publication or hosted operation is authorized. Remaining capabilities are explicitly tracked as open Features; items remain open for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-06T19:43:50.816Z",codex-agent,"Orchestrator opened public PR 1 at the completed implementation head. Resuming review ownership: inspect CodeRabbit including outside-diff and nitpick content, address findings, validate changes, push all package-owned tracker records, and verify final CI. Existing implementation and public proofs remain complete."
  "2026-11-06T19:45:53.798Z",codex-agent,"Review round one is queued for PR 1. Automatic CodeRabbit and Sourcery skips are missing review evidence; both notices received negative reactions. The requested voting script hit a GraphQL API rate limit, so equivalent notice reactions were submitted through REST. No findings or CI failures are currently available; CI jobs are queued. Preserve the completed source validation and wait for the manual review and final-head CI before declaring review complete."
  "2026-11-06T21:10:48.231Z",codex-agent,"Final-head CI passed Node 22, Node 26 and CodeQL on d45600d, while the shared CodeRabbit queue had not reached PR 1. Independent receipt-integrity review then reproduced and fixed a one-to-one outcome-binding gap. Focused native test, linked test, typecheck, lint, duplication, docstrings and five behavioral revert proofs pass. Push the narrow fix, requeue review and rerun both full release checks on the new candidate. Existing public model and byte-reduction results are unchanged."
  "2026-11-07T20:47:21.071Z",codex-agent,"Review round two: CodeRabbit posted 13 unresolved review threads on PR 1 (no outside-diff findings in the review body or PR comments; Sourcery skipped). Resuming the epic's review ownership: verify every thread against current code, fix valid findings with regression tests and behavioral revert proofs, self-review the full PR diff for the same defect classes, run targeted gates plus changelog/identity checks, then push for CI certification of the full release gate."
  "2026-11-08T07:02:12.653Z",codex-agent,"Round two step one is fixed and validated locally: kernel reuse, path-guard scoping and traversal budget landed with three new regression tests; the linked suite passes 69 of 69 tests and the revert acceptance proves 8 red and 8 restored-green behavioral proofs. Remaining round-two work: pack-gate document presence, tightened refusal-code assertions, the writer lock_conflict retry, corpus-privacy import boundaries, public-harness per-test verification with receipt regeneration, live resume-question checks, exact CI runtimes and the linked-test build prefixes."
  "2026-11-08T09:48:51.246Z",codex-agent,"Continuation inspected the existing branch, uncommitted patch, all 13 unresolved threads with complete comments, latest review and tracker records. Retained the three completed fixes and four pending edits in an isolated worktree; no outside-diff findings, no duplicate PR or tracker items. Remaining fixes and final exact-head validation are in progress."
  "2026-11-08T09:57:10.184Z",codex-agent,"All thirteen review findings are valid. Preserved the prior three fixes and completed explicit package-document presence checks, exact native refusal codes, writer contention retries, acquisition import/member restrictions, named concrete harness test results, exact CI runtime provisioning, frozen harness bindings, live current-packet resume questions, and build-prefixed linked commands. Whole-diff follow-up found and fixed cache hits bypassing strict input validation and synthetic public URL literals violating the tracked privacy gate. Public harness regeneration passes three selected tests and reproduces one historical regression, followed by restored success. Remaining work: behavioral revert certification, linked execution and complete npm/Bun release gates."
  "2026-11-08T10:01:35.401Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert certification passed: 18 isolated mutants fail and all 18 restored implementations pass. Covered prior tuple/replay/CAS/budget/receipt guards; public path, shared-DAG work bound and deterministic reuse; required packed docs; acquisition named imports and member calls; concrete selected harness results; frozen receipt bindings; lock retries; CI runtime refusal; live packet answers; and validation before both cache lookups. Four clean-dist linked commands fail without their build prefix and pass with it. Three injected wrong native/domain error codes fail the strengthened assertions and pass after restoration. Every temporary change was confined to disposable copies; package source/history was not altered by proofs. A normal-home health check discovered an unrelated globally installed extension version skew; the isolated-home authoritative tracker check passes without dependency or threshold changes."
  "2026-11-08T10:24:08.941Z",codex-agent,"Final local release certification: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed all 14 stages via pinned pm test --run --progress in isolated homes/Git configuration. Each measured 75 tests, zero failures/skips, 100 percent coverage of 560 statements/306 branches/167 functions/446 lines across eight runtime modules; 98 documented declarations; zero duplication at the unchanged zero threshold; zero production vulnerabilities; 41 allowlisted packed files. Packed acceptance passed 31 CLI commands per package manager, SDK checks, and both SDK/CLI checks on exact Node 22.19.0 and 26.13.0 under each manager. Each full gate passed 18 red/18 restored-green behavioral proofs, four clean-dist build-prefix proofs and three wrong-error-code probes. Final paired-receipt/privacy assertions separately passed seven focused tests; three helper tests also pass on the minimum Node runtime. Earlier gate attempts exposed duplicated proof scaffolding, now factored out; the final gates pass without changed thresholds. Existing local extension skew is avoided by the required isolated home. Final commit/CI verification follows; items remain in_progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-08T10:24:10.158Z",codex-agent,"Thread mapping, all valid: PRRT_kwDOVlkMx860uigS build-prefixed linked commands; PRRT_kwDOVlkMx860uigp independently frozen corpus/receipt/outcome bindings; PRRT_kwDOVlkMx860uigv required packed proof documents; PRRT_kwDOVlkMx860uig1 bounded deterministic reuse with validation before lookup and isolated copies; PRRT_kwDOVlkMx860uig6 public URL/relative path allowance; PRRT_kwDOVlkMx860uihC aggregate shared-subtree traversal bound; PRRT_kwDOVlkMx860uihM explicit writer lock/revision retries; PRRT_kwDOVlkMx860uihW native item_not_found assertion; PRRT_kwDOVlkMx860uihd acquisition import/namespace/member restrictions; PRRT_kwDOVlkMx860uihk exact missing-related/native input refusals; PRRT_kwDOVlkMx860uihs provisioned exact CI runtimes with missing-runtime refusal; PRRT_kwDOVlkMx860uihy concrete named-test events before a pass receipt; PRRT_kwDOVlkMx860uih3 ten live packet questions and measured bytes. Latest review had no outside-diff findings. Review threads were not replied to or resolved. Additional whole-diff fixes cover cache-validation bypass and synthetic-fixture privacy-gate compatibility. No pm CLI/SDK defects were found."
  "2026-11-08T10:39:08.923Z",codex-agent,"Remote verification of source commit 09de2aff8ded90bfdb1cdc81789b4f2918791d05: CodeQL passed (https://github.com/unbraind/pm-case/actions/runs/42471346907). CI attempt 1 failed in Setup Bun on both Node jobs before package installation or checks: the upstream Bun release archive download returned HTTP 504 on every built-in retry (https://github.com/unbraind/pm-case/actions/runs/42471346892/attempts/1). Both exact Node acceptance runtimes were provisioned successfully. Failed jobs were retried on the unchanged source head; attempt 2 is queued at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-case/actions/runs/42471346892/attempts/2. Remote package certification is therefore pending, not a pass. All local 14-stage npm/Bun gates and 75-test source results remain valid. Final captured package has 41 files and SHA-256 0d66b1061c47154319b4f1d5b6872a18efd71b1f97c343649830baec25891d6e, byte-identical to the npm-validated artifact. All 13 original review threads remain unresolved as instructed, with no new threads; CodeRabbit and Sourcery skipped renewed review, so fresh external review evidence is missing. This final tracker-only handoff records the infrastructure blocker for the orchestrator; its new head requires fresh remote CI evidence."
  "2026-11-08T14:49:13.345Z",codex-agent,"Re-review continuation: reuse existing PR 1 and epic, preserve prior commits; branch matches remote and contains origin/main. Four valid classes: prerequisite-complete archive instructions, consistent transient native contention metadata, stored-state validation separated from submission guards across every kernel/API read path, and finite contention retries. Audit SDK/CLI JSON/TOON, packed npm/Bun consumers and real non-git trackers; add adversarial regressions and isolated revert proofs before full gates. Previous head 4f3f70e now has successful Node 22 and Node 26 CI jobs, resolving the earlier evidence-only runtime blocker. No outside-diff findings in latest review."
  "2026-11-08T14:55:29.217Z",codex-agent,"Class audit completed across all runtime modules and documentation: only new submissions run guardSubmitted; every stored normalization, domain enumeration and cover generation now propagates stored mode through reads, proposals, select/record preflight, coverage, explanation, packets and recovery. Cache validation remains strict for new submissions. Transient metadata is centralized in CaseRefusal and preserved through native conversion and JSON/TOON. Writer retries now have validated finite caps, preserve the last failure and invoke conflict callbacks only before another attempt; worker processes have a timeout and pagination tests assert bounded progress. No additional archive-install sites or unbounded contention loops remain. Focused linked test command passed 51/51; typecheck, lint, zero-duplication and docstrings pass. Added packed npm/Bun legacy-state and strict-resubmission journeys without Git. Initial revert proof harness required an assertion wrapper for expected privacy refusals; rerunning the unchanged failure checks after that correction."
  "2026-11-08T14:59:04.873Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: npm run test:revert passed 31 isolated red mutants and 31 restored-green reruns, plus 4 clean-dist build-prefix proofs and 3 wrong-error-code probes. New mutants independently remove the README archive prerequisite, lock_conflict retry metadata, finite writer attempt guard, and each of ten stored-mode handoffs in normalizeModel, enumerateFeasibleTuples, generateCover, readState, evaluateCaseCoverage and API proposal/select/explain. All mutations run in disposable copies; fixed source and history remain intact. These adversarial tests also prove new submissions still refuse after legacy data warms both caches. Full npm and Bun release checks are now running sequentially through pinned pm linked tests, with isolated home/Git configuration and unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-11-08T15:15:14.586Z",codex-agent,"Final re-review gates: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed all 14 stages via pinned pm test --run --progress, sequentially with isolated home/Git configuration and at most 2 test workers. Each passed 79/79 tests with zero failures/skips; 100 percent coverage of 560 statements, 309 branches, 167 functions and 446 lines across 8 runtime modules; 98 documented declarations; zero duplication across 51 sources and zero production vulnerabilities. Each passed packed acceptance: 41 allowlisted files, 42 CLI commands per npm/Bun consumer journey, SDK checks, and exact Node 22.19.0/26.13.0 SDK/CLI checks without Git on PATH. Each also passed 31 red/31 restored-green behavioral mutants, 4 clean-build proofs and 3 wrong-error-code probes. Retained ignored archive matches the validated consumer artifact: SHA-256 26ac5778de2ba5b18024efb64047864b0cfccaf10a34a80c2cf4d3fab3d66cb7. Prior focused linked suite passed 51/51. No pm CLI/SDK defect or new out-of-scope work was found; final-head external CI/review follows the push at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-case/pull/1/checks."
  "2026-11-08T15:15:15.781Z",codex-agent,"Thread dispositions, all valid: PRRT_kwDOVlkMx861ACNS fixes prerequisite-complete archive instructions (review.test.ts archive prerequisite regression); PRRT_kwDOVlkMx861ACNU fixes consistent transient refusal metadata across native conversion and JSON/TOON (review.test.ts metadata table); PRRT_kwDOVlkMx861ACNZ separates trusted persisted validation from new-submission policy throughout SDK/CLI reads and writes (review.test.ts legacy-state regression, ten independent handoff mutants, packed npm/Bun journeys); PRRT_kwDOVlkMx861ACNa bounds contention retries while retaining final error identity (writer-retry.test.ts cap corpus and mutant), adds worker timeout and pagination progress assertions. Existing PRRT_kwDOVlkMx860uihs runtime-provisioning implementation remains valid; prior head 4f3f70e passed both CI Node jobs and both new local full gates again exercised both exact runtimes for each manager. No finding was refused. Threads are intentionally left untouched for orchestrator replies and bot verification."
  "2026-11-08T16:32:00.367Z",codex-agent,"Continuation at existing PR #1 head 1378cab. Reusing the clean review worktree and existing epic; main is already included. Auditing all five open threads and sibling classes: bounded scan work, home privacy aliases, stored-state compatibility, install initialization, exact runtimes, portable harness commands, and non-vacuous revert/import proofs. No review-thread actions or duplicate PR/items."
  "2026-11-08T16:40:27.912Z",codex-agent,"Class audit: request validation now has a 4 Mi-character aggregate text budget and a single home classifier covering dotted aliases, WSL/UNC mounts, normalized paths and configured/resolved homes. Stored-state normalization remains separate and retains SDK/CLI/JSON/TOON/no-Git coverage, including packed npm/Bun consumers. Proof counts derive from frozen scenarios; the explicit 50 percent byte reduction contract is retained unchanged and framing regeneration is documented. Harnesses use the platform PATH delimiter and default shell; CI/release provision Node 22.19.0, Node 26.13.0 and Bun 1.3.5. The older unresolved install-runtime thread is covered too. Production/acquisition import guards include optional/member/dynamic shapes. Focused class suite passed 15/15; typecheck and lint pass; removing duplicated proof helpers before full gates."
  "2026-11-08T16:41:57.815Z",codex-agent,"Pinned pm CLI UX observation: a multiline key=value files input was accepted as a literal final-row path including scope syntax. Removed that unintended link with a quoted path and used repeated --add-glob entries; immutable history is retained. All 37 current links validate. No upstream issue was filed per this task scope."
  "2026-11-08T16:59:50.784Z",codex-agent,"Focused final class command ran through pinned pm test --run --only-last --progress: 18/18 passed. Preliminary complete coverage passed 87/87 with exactly 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines over all nine production modules; no ignored sources or threshold changes. Preliminary disposable reverts passed 43 named assertion mutations with baseline=0, reverted=1, restored=0, plus four build/import checks and three wrong-code probes. Two further optional/member import mutants were added for the final full gates. A transient AST test-helper failure on numeric property keys was corrected and the passing focus rerun; production behavior was unaffected."
  "2026-11-08T17:32:22.765Z",codex-agent,"Additional README smoke verification found a valid adapter defect: createDirectoryHost supplied the same relative tracker path as both cwd and pmRoot, causing tracker_root_missing. The directory adapter now resolves that operator path once and binds the native client, ID normalization and settings reads to the same absolute root. No content guard is applied to operator paths. A new non-Git SDK lifecycle regression changes cwd after construction and checks all reads/writes and JSON/TOON output. Packed npm/Bun SDK consumers now use relative roots. The earlier npm full gate passed, but Bun validation was deliberately interrupted when this new defect was found; both final gates will be rerun on the corrected implementation."
  "2026-11-08T17:39:37.586Z",codex-agent,"The expanded pinned pm focus passed 22/22. The README SDK bootstrap now passes verbatim with a relative tracker root in a fresh non-Git directory. Five separate adapter mutations were each baseline-green, named assertion-red, restored-green: root normalization, native client root, ID settings root, section settings root, and the old raw core-settings read. The settings oracle uses an explicit non-default section value, so a fallback cannot pass vacuously. Directory SDK consumers in both packed managers now use relative roots. Typecheck, lint and zero-duplication gates pass. Final full npm and Bun gates are restarting with frozen production/test source; the durable revert harness now contains 50 behavioral mutations."
  "2026-11-08T18:04:44.052Z",codex-agent,"Final verification on frozen production and test source:\n- npm run release:check: passed in 731 seconds.\n- bun run release:check: passed in 659 seconds.\n- Each: 88/88 tests with zero skipped/todo/canceled; 596/596 statements, 332/332 branches, 169/169 functions, 482/482 lines over all nine runtime modules. Thresholds and source inventory remain unchanged.\n- Each: 45 allowlisted packed files; 50 CLI commands per manager, npm/Bun SDK and JSON/TOON journeys without Git, exact Node 22.19.0 and 26.13.0 under both managers; zero production vulnerabilities; zero duplication; 100 documented declarations. Native real-event baseline/failure readers also passed directly on both exact Node versions.\n- Each full gate ran npm run test:revert / bun run test:revert: 50 behavioral mutations, each with passing named baseline, named assertion failure after mutation, restored passing result; four linked clean-dist build proofs; three wrong-error-code probes. Disposable copies only. Final pinned pm focus: 22/22.\n\nThread -> general rule -> fix / failing regression:\nPRRT_kwDOVlkMx860uihs -> runtime claims require exact provisioning -> CI and release provision/retain both exact Node runtimes and pin Bun 1.3.5; all CI and release jobs provision their exact acceptance runtimes.\nPRRT_kwDOVlkMx861B3Gy -> bound cumulative submitted scanning work -> shared four-Mi-code-unit budget counts repeated strings/subtrees before scanning; aggregate text work counts repeated strings and shared subtrees before any write.\nPRRT_kwDOVlkMx861B3G3 -> provenance must explain intentional acquisition scope -> tracker-only harvest and full-tree execution use the same frozen revision; harness archives share frozen provenance while retaining intentional path scopes.\nPRRT_kwDOVlkMx861B3G7 -> use platform PATH conventions everywhere -> delimiter in both harnesses, AST guard across all runtime/scripts/test files including array joins; harness PATH composition and linked commands use platform conventions.\nPRRT_kwDOVlkMx861B3G_ -> explicit release contracts and corpus-derived non-vacuity -> unchanged 50-percent reduction threshold documented with framing/receipt regeneration; corpus-derived question/harness counts and adversarial receipt checks; all documented CLI and SDK installs initialize a tracker before package use plus live ten-question packet proof.\nPRRT_kwDOVlkMx861B3HC -> use the platform shell for linked commands -> default-shell execution replaces the POSIX-only launcher, with baseline before each proof; harness PATH composition and linked commands use platform conventions.\n\nShared-class closure also includes dotted home aliases with an index loop (including long punctuation), WSL/UNC and resolved home roots, unchanged stored-state read compatibility, complete production/acquisition member/optional/dynamic import guards, and real README CLI/SDK initialization. The added directory-host lifecycle catches relative-root drift and raw core-settings reads using an explicit non-default extension section, with five independent source reverts. Packed SDK consumers exercise relative roots. No finding was refused. Review threads remain untouched for the orchestrator; no merge or release."
  "2026-11-08T18:06:44.031Z",codex-agent,"Environment boundary: post-handoff tracker health with inherited global extensions reports pm-github host-version skew (pinned package host 2026.11.5 versus extension host 2026.11.7). Both complete final gates passed with isolated homes and Git configuration; final metadata health is checked under that same CI isolation. This is an inherited global integration warning, not a reason to change the pinned dependency or global services in this PR. Full source evidence is unchanged."
